        "alt": "An open shaggy mane cap has an inky black rim and hanging black strand, with a smaller white closed cap in front."
      },
      "visibleEvidence": "A mature open cap with a black rim, a long black strand descending from its margin, and a younger white cylindrical cap in front. The strand and age contrast remain legible in the published hires file.",
      "fictionalContext": "Remembered opening sequence, expectation and desire to reassure are fiction. The younger cap is an anonymous neighbor, not proven offspring or the same mycelium. The body is maturing and deliquescing, not recovering from injury.",
      "status": "proposed; independent lead review required"
    },
    {
      "id": "botanical40-02",
      "characterId": "sylvia-bead",
      "subject": "wrinkled peach mushroom",
      "species": "Rhodotus palmatus",
      "platform": "instagram",
      "contentType": "post",
      "theme": "sensory",
      "title": "A little overdressed",
      "body": "I was pleased when the amber beads appeared on my stem. They went beautifully with the pink cap.\n\nThen more came. Several ran together, and the lowest began to stretch.\n\nFor a while I tried to think of myself as richly decorated. There is now a large drop preparing to fall off the bottom of me.\n\nI would have preferred to remain ornamental for a little longer.",
      "mediaSha1": "ba9242211a68b65a99eb16f5559de43285d35161",
      "media": {
        "id": "botanical40-02",
        "imageUrl": "https://www.nps.gov/articles/images/Rhodotus_palmatusE.jpg",
        "sourceUrl": "https://www.nps.gov/articles/so-many-mushrooms.htm",
