        "rightsEvidence": "NPS/Sarah Daugherty staff credit and monitoring work identified in article; NPS ownership disclaimer",
        "sourceLocal": "/tmp/botanical40/mushrooms.html",
        "licenseUrl": "https://www.nps.gov/aboutus/disclaimer.htm",
        "alt": "A pink wrinkled-peach mushroom grows from decaying wood, with large amber droplets along its pale stem."
      },
      "visibleEvidence": "Pink reticulated cap, pale stem with many rounded amber drops and a larger pendant drop low on the stem. The source specifically identifies guttation.",
      "fictionalContext": "Earlier small beads, merging drops and preference for an ornamental appearance are fiction grounded in the visible secreting structure. No distress, rainstorm or insect visitor is invented.",
      "status": "proposed; independent lead review required"
    }
